  "body": "## What\n\nDefine the proposed Assisted-by convention with an explicit catalog of 124 harness/version/model/effort tuples, distinct agent IDs, exact commit-to-PR unions, and squash propagation. Publish the reserved workflow-reference provenance section and decision index entry. Cover coordinator notes, issue comments, Project drafts, and field-edit records.\n\n## Why\n\nIssue #131 requires mechanically checkable provenance. The original five examples did not define catalog admission and omitted required reference/linking artifacts. This revision supplies those artifacts while retaining the current prohibition until #134.\n\n## Evidence\n\nHarness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: gpt-6-astra, medium effort.\n\n- [Source evidence and validation](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/decision/131-assisted-by-convention/research/gates/assisted-by/evidence.md) records the reproduced omissions, pinned Linux/Git passages, coordinator notes, and validation limits.\n- [Proposed verifier cases](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/decision/131-assisted-by-convention/research/gates/assisted-by/examples.md) cover catalog admission, contributor unions, comments, Project edits, linking alternatives, and cutover cases.\n- The document-completeness probe failed before the fix and passed afterward. Catalog expansion confirms 124 unique tuples, including Sol-medium, with unsupported model/effort pairs refused. These are specification checks, not a runtime provenance verifier.\n- Local mutation, binary build, docs build, formatting, prose checks, and secret scans passed. Local aggregate checks were interrupted after prolonged silence in coverage (exit 130). CI ran the aggregate successfully on dcece1f. Local rendered-link checking hit the Chromium sandbox denial; the CI docs job passed.\n- Merged current main without conflicts in 01993ee. No history was rewritten.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe decision and workflow reference now define the provenance contract. The reference section is published at the path reserved by #131. When #84/PR #137 integrates its full-page generator, it must preserve or render this section.\n\nIssue #124 has no selected linking policy in the inspected records. Examples cover both its closing-keyword and explicit-automation options, retain Refs for the completed issue, and distinguish related issues that remain open. Conformance to a final #124 selection remains unverified. This PR does not activate closure or attribution policy.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] CI green at 1a1b08a: check, docs, pr-body, imported-research, mutation\n- [x] Decision, provenance reference, index, and conditional linking examples updated\n- [x] No secrets found\n- [x] Evidence committed\n- [ ] Final #124 policy selection available for conformance review\n\nRefs: #131\n",
